Through the interviews I completed, I talked to like-minded, same-aged peers who experience executive dysfunction in their day-to-day activities. Something similar among all interviewees is that they all have a habit of doomscrolling when tasks have to be completed, however, they take the necessary breaks needed in order for them to completed successfully. Procrastination is at all all time high and it's said that parallel play does help with completing these tasks. What did surprise me is one of my interviewees read instead of doomscrolling which I assumed wouldn't be the case. The balance between finding leisure time and daily duties is the problem at hand. 
